## 1 · 26c-02 — three totals for §32.1.4 stand at once, and the Register records a change the volume never received

**What the volume prints.** Main **L8978**: *"**Fifty-five cells are named and nobody has put anything in
them.**"* Main **L8999** (§32.1.4.1, *Which of this book's numbers hold still*): *"§32.1.4 counts fifty-five cells
named and unoccupied. **Recomputed now the total is 48**, and the movement is the finding rather than the
correction."*

**What the Register records.** **373**: *"§32.1.4's fifty-five is 48 today … §32.1.4.1 names three more that are
still asserted and should not be, and leaves that undone rather than claiming it."* **375**: *"**§32.1.4's
fifty-five is 47 today** and **is no longer written as a number**; what the section asserts instead is the shape,
which does not move: **Λ contributes none, the audit set seventeen, the numbers index the largest share, Q and the
mathematics four each.**"*

**Measured.** Three totals are live simultaneously — **55** (main L8978, printed as a word), **48** (§32.1.4.1
L8999 and register 373), **47** (register 375). The replacement *shape* sentence register 375 says the section
now asserts appears in **no volume**. Register 375 states the number is *no longer written as a number*; L8978
still writes it as one.

**Why it is the largest of the four.** A change the Register records and the volume did not receive is the mirror
image of a silent change: the record is ahead of the artefact rather than behind it. Register 375 also carries
§32.1.4's total into the six build readouts of §2.21, so on 375's own account the figure should be press-computed
and not typed at all.

**The ruling.** One of:

- **(a) The section takes the change 375 records** — L8978's *Fifty-five* is replaced by the shape sentence and
  the total becomes a press readout, §32.1.4.1's *48* re-stated or dropped as superseded. A new Register entry
  citing 373 and 375 seats it. *Consequence:* the three totals collapse to one live readout; §32.1.4.1's "the
  movement is the finding" survives as history.
- **(b) 375 is corrected by a new entry citing it** — the change 375 announced was not made and the entry says so.
  *Consequence:* the printed 55 stands with 48 beside it, and 47 is withdrawn as a figure that was computed but
  never landed.
- **(c) A third state you name.**

*Docket 23 / 35 / 12.* Adjacent and not part of this ruling: **26c-01** (F.4.1's *method ratio* is named in exactly
one Register site, 296, which carries no numeral) and **26c-03** (nineteen PP-only figures with no Register site,
sixteen of them in no volume at all, to be read against §2.21). Both wait behind this one.

